A||||7||ejayerik||Good trade?||||5||
Z||000000||ejayerik||12-07-2001||08:40 PM||||Hey, some guy wants to trade my 88 Z24 for an 88 GT Fiero that has been wrecked. It has a good engine with only 33 thousand on it. The whole front end is beond repair. But the rest of the car, including the interior is in great shape. What do you ppl think? Good trade? My Z24 is on it's last leg engine wise. It is sitting around waiting to be rebuilt. I guess thats what happens when you have spun barrings.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><BR>here is the pic: <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpics.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=118" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpics.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=118</A> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cheever3000||12-07-2001||09:48 PM||||Depends... is he already a Forum member?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Can't be one of us if he's getting <B>rid</B> of a Fiero!  Therefore I think I can safely guess that most of the votes hereafter will be in favor of the trade!  And you'll start getting to know us very well.  So, welcome!  (BTW, that does look like a nice car)<P>||||reg||5
Z||000002||4BanGinFun||12-07-2001||11:30 PM||||nice cav man its a good trade if you can find a fiero in need of a engine thats in good shape but i do have to say if that cav was a coupe id take it off your hands  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> . 5spd??? 3.1???? nice anyway<P>oh welcome!<P>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P><BR>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/||||reg||6
Z||000003||FieroMontreal||12-08-2001||12:12 AM||||At first I was thinking go for the trade! Then I saw the picture.. that Z24 looks really nice.. I don't know what I would do.. do you already own another Fiero because if not a wrecked GT won't do you any good. Can you get us pictures of this GT? It would be a lot easier for us to evaluate the situation.<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ejayerik||12-08-2001||09:12 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ejayerik:<BR><B>Hey, some guy wants to trade my 88 Z24 for an 88 GT Fiero that has been wrecked. It has a good engine with only 33 thousand on it. The whole front end is beond repair. But the rest of the car, including the interior is in great shape. What do you ppl think? Good trade? My Z24 is on it's last leg engine wise. It is sitting around waiting to be rebuilt. I guess thats what happens when you have spun barrings.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">  <BR>here is the pic: <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpics.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=118" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpi  cs.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=118</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry, no pics of the Fiero. And yes, I own an 85 2M4 with a 5-speed trans. The Fiero wrecked pretty much up to the dash. I am not sure if the driver made it out alive. The guy is not a part of this forum and he bought it at auction. BTW..here is some more pics of the Z24. And it is only the 2.8 Automatic. (you take what you can get) But I did all the suspension work on it myself. <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpics.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=113" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpi cs.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=113</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpics.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=116" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpi cs.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=116</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpics.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=117" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/ejayerikxtechnotranceplace/ejayspersonalpi cs.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&PhotoID=117</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by ejayerik (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||12-08-2001||09:31 AM||||Hmmm... don't think I'd trade.  Maybe just offer to buy it from him!  Although with a bad motor- the cav might not be worth much to you. But the 88 GT really is probably only good to strip parts from. It's a tossup!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||12-08-2001||10:13 AM||||I wouldn't take the trade. Just buy it.<BR>The wrecked GT is probably worth about $500-600, tops. If you can get it for that much or less, and part it out, you might be able to make a little bit of profit. That's if the drivetrain, rear clip and interior are all in good shape. (I paid $450 for a similarly wrecked Formula, and have an 88 coupe to transplant the Formula drivetrain, cradle and all, into.) Naked fastback clips go for $200+. A complete conversion, with tail lights, wiring, and all the bits and pieces can go for substantially more. <BR>If you are considering a swap into your 85, it can be done, but you're going to have to scrounge mounts, and maybe some wiring. You <I>can</I> install the entire 88 rear cradle with adapters from Held Motorsports, but it will require you to use coil-overs. There isn't enough room in the 84-87 shock towers for the stock 88 springs. <BR>I believe the Fiero shortblock will fit your Cav (nice looking car, BTW).<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever3000||12-08-2001||03:56 PM||||If the wreckage is that bad, don't trade.<BR>Can you get the VIN number for us?  We have a member, "88 Database Guy", who keeps track of them.  It would be very much appreciated.<BR>||||reg||1
